  "title": "Buffers Summary",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "A solution containing a mixture of a weak acid and its conjugate base, or of a weak base and its conjugate acid, is called a "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "buffer solution"
              },
              {
                "text": ". The presence of a weak conjugate acid–base pair provides reactants that may neutralize small additions of strong acid or base, yielding weaker conjugate partners. The hydronium ion concentration of a buffer solution therefore does not change significantly when a small amount of acid or base is added."
              }
            ],
            "id": "pi5my7jni0jpxjn",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
